---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cite from '../components/Cite.astro';
import Grade from '../components/Grade.astro';
import { comparison } from '../data/comparison';
---
<Base
  terms
  title="Cross-institutional comparison"
  description="Harvard’s Program for Evolutionary Dynamics, the MIT Media Lab and Harvard Medical School compared on funding, access, DNA activity and institutional response."
  eyebrow="Comparison"
  lede="Three places, one donor, three different patterns. The table uses the same questions for each so the differences are visible."
  reviewed="2026-11-20"
  basis="Harvard’s 2020 report; MIT’s 2020 report; CNN and STAT"
  toc={false}
>
  <div class="table-wrap full">
    <table class="stack">
      <caption>Each cell is sourced. On a phone, the table becomes one card per question.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Element</th>{comparison.columns.map((c) => <th>{c}</th>)}</tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {comparison.rows.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <th>{r.element}</th>
            {r.cells.map((cell, i) => (
              <td data-label={comparison.columns[i]}>
                <Fragment set:html={cell.text} />{cell.cites.map((id) => <Cite id={id} />)}
                {cell.grade && <> <Grade g={cell.grade} /></>}
              </td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="reading">Reading the table</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Harvard’s program</strong> is the deepest relationship: the largest gift, the most visits, and the only one with standing physical access. It involved no direct money after 2008 and no genetic activity.</li>
    <li><strong>MIT’s Media Lab</strong> is smaller in every measure but is the only one of the three that accepted his own money after the conviction, with the knowledge of senior administrators.</li>
    <li><strong>Harvard Medical School</strong> is where the genetics contact sits. The one confirmed sequencing job was invoiced by a hospital physician who was not a Harvard employee.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Both institutional reports were written before the 2026 document release. Each university has since faced reporting
    that its review was incomplete, and Harvard’s second review had not reported when this page was last
    checked.<Cite id="crimson-2026-hms-rating" /><Cite id="tech-2026-mit" />
  </p>
</Base>
